      "level": 2,
      "content": "PART I — ANCIENT INDIA"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Ancient Indian history saw pivotal encounters like Alexander's invasion at Hydaspes (326 BCE) and Emperor Ashoka's conversion after the Kalinga War (261 BCE).",
        "Medieval battles, including Tarain (1191–1192) and First Panipat (1526), reshaped northern power dynamics and established foreign dynasties.",
        "The 18th century transition marked the decline of regional empires and the rise of the British East India Company through Plassey (1757) and Buxar (1764).",
        "Colonial expansion culminated in Anglo-Mysore, Anglo-Maratha, and Anglo-Sikh wars, consolidating British supremacy over the subcontinent."
      ],
      "id": "yo9lzah"
    },
